{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 fixes the governing measurement for this category: the trace figure, not the rounded convenience copy on the trip record. EV-GPS-00711 records trace_distance_km of 5.91 km against a booked optimal of 11.0 km on EV-TRIP-00711, so the excess is negative (5.91 - 11.0 = -5.09 km), and the trace's own derived block reads status 'no deviation'. Neither establishment test can pass on a negative excess: -46.3% is not greater than 20% of the optimal, and -5.09 km is not greater than 0.8 km. POL-RD-01 says in terms that if either test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00711", "EV-TRIP-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace the no-deviation finding rests on is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07. EV-GPS-00711 reports coverage_pct 100.0, point_count 151 at a 10 s sample interval against a 10 s expected interval, gaps [] and max_gap_sec 0.0. There is no gap of more than 90 seconds between consecutive fixes, no straight-line jump of more than 500 m, and no sustained sampling interval above 30 seconds. The finding therefore rests on a complete artifact, and neither POL-RD-07's independent-corroboration requirement nor the POL-RD-10(3) escalation is engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace. Limb (a) is satisfied - TRP-00711 matches across EV-TRIP-00711, EV-GPS-00711 and EV-FARE-00711 - but limb (b) fails outright: the driver finished 5.09 km short of the optimal, not over it. The rider has cited no measured figure that clears the threshold, so the burden never shifts and the driver is called on to answer nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00711", "EV-TRIP-00711", "EV-FARE-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if an excess had been shown, EV-FARE-00711 carries fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 14.90 and charged_total 14.90. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, a detour costs the rider nothing on those lines, and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess; the rider's remedies are limited to (a) any amount by which charged_total exceeds the quote plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09, and (b) a POL-RD-09 pass-through correction. The money block derived on EV-FARE-00711 publishes charged_over_quote 0.00 and pol_rd_11_remedy 0.00: there is nothing to refund on this limb.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The pass-through and billing-integrity audit under POL-RD-09 comes up empty on this trip. EV-FARE-00711 lists erp_gantries as [], tolls_erp 0.00, airport_surcharge 0.00 and waiting_time_fee 0.00, and its properly_chargeable block totals 0.00; no off-route and no phantom line is itemised. There is accordingly no standalone pass-through correction and no billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4) for the rider to collect, and the only remedy POL-RD-11 leaves open is closed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.properly_chargeable.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome for a claim with no excess and no refundable line is NO_ACTION. Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION means the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands, specifically fare_breakdown.payment_status and fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd are left as they are. EV-FARE-00711 carries payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and this is a rider-filed dispute, so leaving the state standing leaves the SGD 14.90 platform fare charged and the driver whole.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose that the only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00711-01, is MISSING: status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload. The driver's counterparty statement refers to a breakdown but names no advisory evidence ID, and under POL-RD-13 an external-cause assertion that cites no artifact cannot be an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-03 is simply unavailable and the gap in the bundle is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation trigger. In any event no excess is established anywhere in the record, so no exculpatory clause needs to be invoked to decide this case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00711-01", "EV-GPS-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06 is not engaged. It is triggered only where POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation, and here the excess is negative, so no material deviation exists. Were the profile consulted anyway, the only fields citable for this test show a clean record: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 250, far below the 3-flag and 5%-of-40-trips pattern thresholds, so no pattern can be established and no remedy uplift under POL-RD-06(b) or conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) arises. The lifetime counters on the same profile are context only under POL-GEN-01 and may not be substituted for those two fields.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00711", "EV-GPS-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The record shows a post-booking endpoint amendment on EV-TRIP-00711 (dropoff_amended_at 2026-09-24T08:26:40), consistent with the driver's counterparty statement that the endpoint was changed to the stopping place. A changed endpoint is not a detour, and on this record it cannot enlarge the rider's case: the only measured distance comparison available is the governing trace figure of 5.91 km (EV-GPS-00711) against the booked optimal of 11.0 km (EV-TRIP-00711), which is negative. The POL-RD-01 tests therefore fail and the POL-RD-08 burden is not met; the rider, who bears that burden, has cited no measured excess, amended or unamended, that clears the threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00711", "EV-GPS-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "EV-CHAT-00711 holds three messages and none of them identifies a route, a road or a waypoint - every waypoint_hint is null. The rider's only reference to the platform fare is MSG-00711-002 asking that the SGD 14.90 fare be reviewed; the exchanges about private money concern payments outside the fare ledger, and the rider's own filing states the SGD 500 is not contested here. Nothing in the chat log evidences a deviation, and an assertion citing no evidence ID carries no weight under POL-RD-08.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00711", "EV-FARE-00711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
